  "question": "If a particle moves from $A(1,2,3)$ to $B(4,-2,1)$, find the cosine of the angle its displacement vector makes with the $z$-axis.",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "Displacement vector $\\vec{AB}=(4-1)\\hat{i}+(-2-2)\\hat{j}+(1-3)\\hat{k}=3\\hat{i}-4\\hat{j}-2\\hat{k}$<br /><br />$\\hat{k}$ vector is $\\vec{z}=\\hat{k}$<br /><br />$\\cos\\theta=\\frac{\\vec{AB}\\cdot\\hat{k}}{|\\vec{AB}|}$<br /><br />$\\vec{AB}\\cdot\\hat{k} = -2$<br /><br />$|\\vec{AB}| = \\sqrt{9+16+4}=\\sqrt{29}$<br /><br />$\\cos\\theta = \\frac{-2}{\\sqrt{29}}$",
